## Rule 1: Naming Conventions (Java/camelCase)

### Variables & Methods
```java
// ✅ CORRECT - camelCase
private String userName;
public void calculateTotalPrice() { }

// ❌ WRONG
private String user_name;      // snake_case
```

### Classes & Interfaces
```java
// ✅ CORRECT - PascalCase
public class OrderService { }
public interface PaymentRepository { }
```

### Constants
```java
// ✅ CORRECT - UPPER_SNAKE_CASE
public static final String DEFAULT_CURRENCY = "USD";
```

### Method Naming Patterns
| Purpose | Pattern | Example |
|---------|---------|---------|
| Get single | `get` + Entity | `getUser()`, `getOrderById()` |
| Get multiple | `getAll` / `find` | `getAllProducts()`, `findByStatus()` |
| Create | `create` / `save` | `createOrder()`, `saveUser()` |
| Update | `update` | `updateProfile()`, `updateStatus()` |
| Delete | `delete` / `remove` | `deleteOrder()`, `removeItem()` |
| Check | `is` / `has` / `can` | `isValid()`, `hasPermission()` |

